> What did I miss? Why is that working like a charme under Linux and not at all under Windows?


Because Windows is not a unix operating system and is much more limited. Unlike modern operating systems Windows lacks support for copy-on-write forking and thus is limited to a single core for interpreted R.


> Should I expect the right behaviour under MacOSX?
> 

Yes, Mac OS X is a unix OS.


> My question could probably be more detailed, but I suspect this is a very common issue I get here.
> 

Well, you'll find this on the main Rserve page:

"Although Rserve works on Windows it is not recommended to use it on that platform. Windows lacks important features that make the separation of namespaces possible, therefore Rserve for Windows works in cooperative mode only, that is only one connection at a time is allowed and all subsequent connections share the same namespace. Briefly: don't use Windows unless you really have to."

Cheers,
Simon


