> But I don't know how to get the values into the list. I wanted to avoid to create and intermediate column vector for these values. Is it possible? Or do you suggest something complete different?
> 

Ah, if you have to assemble everything in memory in the Java side anyway then you may as well push the entire dataframe directly as you illustrate above. What I was talking about is the case where it makes sense to push the data one vector at a time. The only difference really is the memory usage on the transfer end - the result is the same in either case. With the entire dataframe you'll need 4 * n memory total (2n on each side - one for the data, one for the encoded message), by pushing them one at a time you need 2 * n + 4 * max. column.

Cheers,
Simon



