On Dec 12, 2014, at 4:05 AM, Friedrich Schuster <Friedrich.Schuster at analytical-software.de> wrote:
> 
> 
> Hello, 
>  
> It is possible to initialize the server instance via the “eval” or “source” directives in the config file.
> I can create or load R objects this way, e.g. a large data frame, and it is shared by all forked instances. That works great.
>  
> Is it also possible to modify the objects in the R server environment while the Rserve server process is running? Or has it always to be restartet, when the data has to be updated? (The client sessions will have to be stopped, of course). 

Yes, using control commands (serverEval/serverSource). The existing client sessions don't need to be stopped since they are independent of the server. However, the server will queue up new connection requests until the evaluation finishes.

Note that there is a known bug in the development version of Rserve (1.8) in control commands (since the connection implementation between the clients and the server has been completely rewritten) which can lead to a stalling server, so if you need control commands it's currently advisable to use the 1.7 series where the control commands are stable.

Cheers,
Simon



