From dscheffy at gmail.com  Mon Dec 15 20:20:46 2014
From: dscheffy at gmail.com (Jeff Hansen)
Date: Mon, 15 Dec 2014 14:20:46 -0600
Subject: rJava issues with deserializing objects
Message-ID: <CAA77SLvrQ9VNhsS-qg2z5LRwwcZ8SysHngnu5m_XnQPZ_-1FsQ@mail.gmail.com>

I've run into some problems trying to deserialize model objects created by
RWeka. I have no problem serializing the objects with an ObjectOutputStream
and the writeObject() method, however when I try to deserialize the file I
previously created I get a ClassNotFoundException.

I've traced it back to a relatively long standing issue with the underlying
implementation of ObjectInputStream.resolveClass(). It calls a private
method latestUserDefinedLoader() which in turn calls a native method
sun.misc.VM.latestUserDefinedLoader().

It's not clear to me how this method determines what classloader to use,
but I'm finding in practice that it's never the RJavaClassLoader. So far
the only way I've found to work around the issue is to create my own custom
subclass of ObjectInputStream and override the resolveObject() method to
use a custom specified class loader.

I've pasted sample R and Java code used to illustrate the issue below.

Please let me know if there's a better way to implement this, or if you
have any thoughts on how to make this work more automatically from the
rJava code.

